# Citation metadata for Cell Quant Studio Universal.
# Add a "doi:" line once the release has been archived (for example on Zenodo).
cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this software, please cite it using the metadata below."
title: "Cell Quant Studio Universal"
type: software
version: "2.3.0"
date-released: "2026-11-19"
abstract: >-
  A Fiji/ImageJ application for configurable multichannel fluorescence
  microscopy analysis: channel preparation, independent channel segmentation,
  ROI-based object counts, marker-positive area and intensity measurements,
  folder batch processing, validation against manual annotation, and
  reusable settings profiles.
authors:
  - family-names: "Khimach"
    given-names: "Ivan"
repository-code: "https://github.com/KiViKatt/ImageJ-SingleCellQuantificationPlugin"
license: GPL-3.0-or-later
keywords:
  - "ImageJ"
  - "Fiji"
  - "fluorescence microscopy"
  - "image analysis"
  - "organoids"
  - "segmentation"
